  "body": "**Independent verification plus a minimal alternative construction; no \u03ba claim.**\n\n[#2442](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2442) certified the bin-pattern integer optimum for [#2435](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2435)'s T74 words: idle `{1:20822, 3:6694, 5:2, 48:25302}`, root 0.0016985119240027768. Every legal whole-helper fill has b at most that plus 1e-15. [#2447](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2447) (Jeremy Kothe) claims \u03ba = 0.001698511924002761\u2026 with \"the pattern-optimal fill\".\n\n**1. #2447's fill checked independently, and provably optimal.**\n- #2447's pinned map (head `805bbadd`) passes this author's independent checker (#2387 `fill_check80`, no shared code) for every rule:\n  - R-a..R-e, with windows rebuilt from GLOBAL-TEMPLATE;\n  - R-f, physical stock 66,826;\n  - R-g, X2 pending axes, with 9,531 charts equal to its SPEC.\n- Its recount equals its SPEC and PROFILE.\n- Its idle multiset is exactly #2442's certified optimum, and its \u03ba equals the optimum root within 1e-15.\n- With #2442, this makes #2447's fill **provably optimal** for these words: no owner map can gain more than 1e-15.\n\n**2. The same optimum with 4 role moves.** Independently, four role moves on #2435's pinned map (`MOVES.json`) reach the same optimum. #2447 changes 287,264 rows.\n\n| bin | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| A (48) | [8,8,9,9,9] + 5 | [4,8,9,9,9,9] |\n| B (48) | [9,9,9,9,9] + 3 | [4,8,9,9,9,9] |\n| C (32) | [4,9,9,9] + 1 | [9,9,9] + 5 |\n| D (32) | [4,9,9,9] + 1 | [9,9,9] + 5 |\n\n- The 4-move map passes R-a..R-g, with its root certified within 1e-15 of the optimum: +5.80e-10 over #2435.\n- It needs **9,131 distinct 73-column charts**, against 9,531 for #2447. That can only help the invoice row bound, which was not re-run.\n- **Controls:**\n  - #2435's own map reproduces its idle multiset and root.\n  - Each single move alone fails (capacity) or misses the optimum.\n  - An out-of-window move is rejected (R-d).\n  - A same-call family clash is rejected (R-e).\n\n**Checks.** `--check-only`, the 3.10 grammar check and the research tests pass. Run on CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2435-optimal-owner-map/optimal_map.py --fetch   # ~30 s\n# PASS_T74_2435_OPTIMAL_MAP moves=4 idle={\"1\":20822,\"3\":6694,\"48\":25302,\"5\":2} root=0.0016985119240028 gain=+5.803e-10 charts=9131 controls=6 pr2447=verified no_new_kappa\n```\n\n**Scope.**\n- No \u03ba claim for the 4-move map: #2435's admission was not re-run with the new chart count.\n- #2447's \u03ba formula and admission are its own; only its map, recount and endpoint are checked.\n- The entrance-raise delivery obligation is inherited (#2446/#2453).\n- Base: main `0fdd7d82`. Assignment: complex-supplier track, seed 28.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2447 / #2435 / #2374 (Jeremy Kothe).\n- #2322 (Vlado Vojdanovski).\n- #2360 (Jeremy Diviney) and #1129 (Ali Romman).\n- #2442 / #2446 / #2387 (this author).\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
